Description: Nebula gives your iOS 16 Lock Screen a beautiful music player that fits right in, with big album art, a blur in your song's colors and smart touches everywhere.  PLAYER • Three styles: Compact, Expanded (with a volume slider) or Mini • Light, Dark, Auto, or Artwork, which tints the player with each song's colors • Shuffle and repeat beside the skip buttons, on whichever side you like • The AirPlay button shows what you're listening on: AirPods, Beats, HomePod, headphones, your car or the iPhone itself • Animated waveform, haptic feedback and a draggable progress bar • Works with NextUp 3: its Up Next row shows right in Nebula's player • Tap the song title to open the app that's playing  BIG ALBUM ART • Tap the album art to see it large on your Lock Screen • The screen fills with a colorful blur of the art, with the time and date kept on top • Covers slide to the next song as the music changes  LOCK SCREEN • Replace Apple's player in place, or float Nebula under the clock or above the flashlight and camera • Notifications make room for the player instead of sliding under it • Room for Widgets keeps the player below your Lock Screen widgets • Hide When Paused tucks the player away after a long pause • Optionally hide Apple's player and the "No Older Notifications" text  Every change applies instantly, with no respring. Nebula starts turned off: turn it on in Settings → Nebula.  For iOS 16 on rootless jailbreaks such as Dopamine.
